  "configuration_id": "config_007",
  "reason": "The current best (config_030: scvi_n200, vit_l, avgpool, weighted) achieved 0.7062 acc. With pca_n200, avgpool clearly outperformed transformer (0.6352 vs 0.5988, ~3.6 pp gap), but scvi_n200 produces a fundamentally different, richer latent representation that may interact with aggregation differently. Config_007 changes only aggregation (avgpool→transformer) while holding scvi_n200, vit_l, multiprofile, and weighted fusion constant, giving a clean single-variable test of whether transformer aggregation could exploit the richer scvi embeddings. This is the highest-impact remaining uncertainty: if transformer matches or beats avgpool here, it opens a new architectural direction; if not, we can confidently lock in avgpool and redirect budget to other axes (e.g., image encoder). It is a logical exploitation of the best configuration while still resolving a key design question."
}

